cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "如果你在研究或工程报告中使用了 hsolve，请按以下信息引用。If you use hsolve in research or engineering reports, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "hsolve: a certified shift-invert eigensolver for large sparse Hermitian (indefinite) eigenproblems from electromagnetic simulation"
abstract: >-
  hsolve computes eigenpairs of large sparse Hermitian standard and generalized eigenproblems
  A x = lambda B x with indefinite A and positive definite or indefinite B, as they arise from
  finite-element models of cavities, waveguides and photonic crystals. It combines MUMPS
  symmetric indefinite LDL^T factorizations with its own block Krylov-Schur solvers and, when B is
  positive definite, certifies through Sylvester inertia counts that no eigenvalue in the target
  window was missed. It offers nearest-to-shift, interval (spectrum slicing) and extreme targets,
  multi-threaded, multi-process and optional GPU execution, and command-line and Python interfaces.
authors:
